WEBVTT

00:00:00.563 --> 00:00:04.656
Watch what happens when
I close this discount offer.

00:00:04.656 --> 00:00:07.740
There’s still a clock ticking
right above the price.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.073
That little button in
the corner is Subtext.

00:00:11.073 --> 00:00:15.469
I can leave it closed and hover
over the timer itself.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:18.448
What I want to know is whether
I’d actually lose the deal

00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:20.156
if I walked away and came back tomorrow.

00:00:22.037 --> 00:00:25.092
When I open the panel,
the first thing I get

00:00:25.092 --> 00:00:27.663
is a reading of the whole shop.

00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:29.619
It’s pushing me to buy quickly,

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:31.729
but there’s no company name on the page,

00:00:31.729 --> 00:00:35.619
and it wants payment by
crypto or bank transfer.

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:40.125
Now I can pick one detail and look closer.

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:43.378
For the countdown, there’s a simple test.

00:00:43.378 --> 00:00:45.905
Reload the page and see
whether the clock starts over.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.400
On this article, the thing
that catches my eye is a chart.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.200
The last bar looks about four
times as tall as the first one.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.990
But follow the bars down to the bottom.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:03.130
When I hover, Subtext points out
that the scale starts at eighty.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:05.750
The numbers go from about
eighty-five to a hundred.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.290
That’s a real increase, but a very
different story from quadrupling.
